    "narrative": "The anchor of today\u2019s lineup is undoubtedly **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing the right-hander Bello, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost and holds a distinct BvP advantage, making him the primary catalyst for our run production today. Joining him in the elite tier is **Kyle Tucker** (75.93), who draws a favorable matchup against Nelson and remains a high-floor start despite a mediocre opposing xERA. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** (66.22) rounds out our strongest offensive options; by hitting in the #3 spot, he gains significant leverage over the base projection, effectively capitalizing on the offensive environment to provide us with much-needed stability in the middle of the order.\n\nNavigating the deeper end of the starting nine, we are proceeding with caution. **Jackson Merrill** (51.97) and **Coby Mayo** (49.57) both fall into the marginal category, largely hampered by the formidable presence of Wheeler and Bello, respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.26) also sits in this range; while his talent is undeniable, a brutal matchup against the elite Sale (xERA 2.89) effectively neuters his ceiling today. On the bench, **Miguel Andujar** was the primary consideration for a spot, but his score of 34.66 failed to break our efficiency floor. Given that **Miguel Andujar** faced a significant platoon penalty against Wheeler, we opted to preserve our daily game caps rather than force a sub-40 start. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given our heavy reliance on speed and the scarcity of SBs in the current market. We are closely monitoring the lineup integrity for all starters, particularly as the secondary pieces like **Brayan Rocchio** (49.52) rely on base-running opportunities that could evaporate if the top of the order fails to reach against their respective starters. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** still sidelined on the IL, the margin for error is thin. We are strictly adhering to the 40-point efficiency floor to ensure our remaining utility spots\u2014which might otherwise be filled by **Josh Lowe**, **Heliot Ramos**, or **Nasim Nunez**\u2014are reserved for matchups that offer a statistical probability of contributing to our core categories.",
